> Module Ptc_net

> Using Types

# Premium tax credit, part 3: net PTC, repayment limitation, routing (Form 8962 lines 26 to 29)

Direct File ("DF" below) module `ptc.xml`
(`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/ptc.xml`): facts
`/netPtcAmount` (line 9239), `/netPtcAmountWhenZeroOrPositive` (Form 8962 line 26),
`/netPtcAmountWhenNegative` (line 27), `/ptcRepaymentLimitation` (line 28, with the
six constants `/ptcRepaymentLimitationLessThan{200,300,400}PercentFpl{Single,Other}`),
`/lesserOfNetPtcAmountAndRepaymentLimitation` (line 29). Routing:
`schedule3.xml` `/otherPaymentsAndRefundableCreditsTotal` (Schedule 3 line 15,
Form 1040 line 31) and `schedule2.xml` `/totalAdditionalTaxesOwed`
(Schedule 2 line 3, Form 1040 line 17). Issue #34, scope.md section 6.6. Parts 1
and 2 are `Ptc_family` (#32) and `Ptc_allowed` (#33).

Law and forms: 26 U.S.C. § 36B(f)(2) (`sources/statute/irc-36B.html`),
Instructions for Form 8962 (2024) (`sources/forms-instructions/i8962--2024.pdf`
pp 16 to 17: lines 26 to 29, Table 5), Form 1040 Schedule 2 line 1a and
Schedule 3 line 9 (`f1040s2--2024.pdf`, `f1040s3--2024.pdf`).
Tests: `catala/tests/test_ptc_net.catala_en`. The oracle comparison is the
`calculator` mapping (`make difftest SCOPE=calculator`), where this module feeds
Form 1040 lines 17 and 31.

## 26 U.S.C. § 36B(f)(2) Excess advance payments

"(A) In general. If the advance payments to a taxpayer under section 1412 of the
Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act for a taxable year exceed the credit
allowed by this section (determined without regard to paragraph (1)), the tax
imposed by this chapter for the taxable year shall be increased by the amount of
such excess. (B) Limitation on increase. (i) In general. In the case of a
taxpayer whose household income is less than 400 percent of the poverty line
for the size of the family involved for the taxable year, the amount of the
increase under subparagraph (A) shall in no event exceed the applicable dollar
amount determined in accordance with the following table (one-half of such
amount in the case of a taxpayer whose tax is determined under section 1(c)
for the taxable year): Less than 200% $600; At least 200% but less than 300%
$1,500; At least 300% but less than 400% $2,500. (ii) Indexing of amount [...]
each of the dollar amounts in the table [...] shall be increased [...]. If the
amount of any increase under clause (i) is not a multiple of $50, such increase
shall be rounded to the next lowest multiple of $50."

Section 1(c) is the rate schedule for unmarried individuals other than
surviving spouses and heads of household, so the halved column is the filing
status Single only; every other filing status uses the full amounts.

## Form 8962 lines 26 to 29 and Table 5

Instructions for Form 8962 (2024) pp 16 to 17:

"Line 26. If line 24 is greater than line 25, subtract line 25 from line 24 and
enter the result on line 26. This result is the amount of your PTC that is more
than the APTC paid, your net PTC. This amount will reduce the amount of tax you
must pay with your tax return or increase your refund. Also enter the amount
from line 26 on Schedule 3 (Form 1040), line 9. Skip lines 27 through 29. If
line 24 is equal to line 25, enter -0- on line 26 and skip lines 27 through 29.
[...] Line 27. If line 25 is greater than line 24, subtract line 24 from line 25
and enter the result. Line 28. The excess APTC you must repay may be limited to
the amounts in Table 5. Enter the appropriate amount from Table 5 on line 28.
[...] If your entry on Form 8962, line 5, is 400 or more, there is no repayment
limitation. You must repay the amount shown on line 27. Leave line 28 blank and
enter the amount from line 27 on line 29. [...] Line 29. Enter the smaller of
line 27 or line 28. If line 28 is blank, enter the amount from line 27 on
line 29. Also enter the amount from Form 8962, line 29, on Schedule 2
(Form 1040), line 1a."

Table 5. Repayment Limitation (2024; the statutory $600, $1,500, $2,500
indexed and rounded down to a multiple of $50, halved for Single):

| Line 5 is | Single | Any other filing status |
|---|---|---|
| Less than 200 | $375 | $750 |
| At least 200 but less than 300 | $950 | $1,900 |
| At least 300 but less than 400 | $1,575 | $3,150 |
| 400 or more | none | none |

Routing. Schedule 3 line 9 (net premium tax credit, Form 8962 line 26) is part
of Schedule 3 line 15, which is Form 1040 line 31 (other payments and
refundable credits). Schedule 2 line 1a (Form 8962 line 29) is part of
Schedule 2 line 3 (additional taxes), which is Form 1040 line 17. Line 17 is
added to line 16 to give line 18, the tax the credit limit worksheets (CDCC,
Schedule R, Saver's, CTC/ODC) start from; `Form_1040` does that for its
`total_additional_taxes_owed` slot, so the credit limits include the excess
APTC repayment, as in DF.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_200_single content money equals $375
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_200_other content money equals $750
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_300_single content money equals $950
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_300_other content money equals $1,900
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_400_single content money equals $1,575
declaration ptc_repayment_limit_under_400_other content money equals $3,150
declaration ptc_repayment_percent_first_step content decimal equals 200.0
declaration ptc_repayment_percent_second_step content decimal equals 300.0
declaration ptc_repayment_percent_no_limit content decimal equals 400.0

declaration scope NetPtc:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus (only Single takes the lower column)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # Form 8962 line 5. DF: ptc.xml /householdIncomeAsPercent (Ptc_family)
  input household_income_as_percent content decimal
  # DF: ptc.xml /taxFamilySizeIsZero (Ptc_family)
  input tax_family_size_is_zero condition
  # Form 8962 line 24. DF: ptc.xml /totalPtcAmountAllowed (Ptc_allowed)
  input total_ptc_amount_allowed content money
  # Form 8962 line 25. DF: ptc.xml /totalAptcAmountTaken (Ptc_allowed)
  input total_aptc_amount_taken content money

  # DF: ptc.xml /netPtcAmount (line 24 minus line 25, may be negative)
  output net_ptc_amount content money
  # Form 8962 line 26. DF: ptc.xml /netPtcAmountWhenZeroOrPositive
  output line26 content money
  # Form 8962 line 27. DF: ptc.xml /netPtcAmountWhenNegative
  output line27 content money
  # Form 8962 line 28 (zero stands for a blank line). DF: ptc.xml /ptcRepaymentLimitation
  output line28 content money
  # Form 8962 line 29. DF: ptc.xml /lesserOfNetPtcAmountAndRepaymentLimitation
  output line29 content money
  # Schedule 3 line 9, then line 15 and Form 1040 line 31.
  # DF: schedule3.xml /otherPaymentsAndRefundableCreditsTotal
  output net_ptc_credit content money
  # Schedule 2 line 1a, then line 3 and Form 1040 line 17.
  # DF: schedule2.xml /totalAdditionalTaxesOwed
  output excess_aptc_repayment content money
```

## Lines 26 and 27

```catala
scope NetPtc:
  definition net_ptc_amount equals total_ptc_amount_allowed - total_aptc_amount_taken

  definition line26 equals
    if net_ptc_amount >= $0 then net_ptc_amount else $0

  definition line27 equals
    if net_ptc_amount < $0 then - net_ptc_amount else $0
```

## Line 28: the repayment limitation

DF writes line 28 as $0 when the tax family size is zero (a workaround so that
the line is blank, `ptc.xml` `/ptcRepaymentLimitation`); line 29 then repays all
of line 27. Statute and instructions do not cover family size zero (there is no
poverty line "for the size of the family involved"), and DF's choice repays in
full, so it is kept. Question for the human: confirm.

```catala
scope NetPtc:
  definition line28 equals
    if tax_family_size_is_zero then $0
    else if household_income_as_percent < ptc_repayment_percent_first_step then
      (if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.Single
       then ptc_repayment_limit_under_200_single
       else ptc_repayment_limit_under_200_other)
    else if household_income_as_percent < ptc_repayment_percent_second_step then
      (if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.Single
       then ptc_repayment_limit_under_300_single
       else ptc_repayment_limit_under_300_other)
    else if household_income_as_percent < ptc_repayment_percent_no_limit then
      (if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.Single
       then ptc_repayment_limit_under_400_single
       else ptc_repayment_limit_under_400_other)
    else $0
```

## Line 29 and routing

A blank line 28 (no limitation) means line 29 is line 27. DF
`/lesserOfNetPtcAmountAndRepaymentLimitation` takes the lesser only when
`/ptcRepaymentLimitation` is non-zero; the table amounts are all positive, so
"line 28 is $0" and "line 28 is blank" coincide.

```catala
scope NetPtc:
  definition line29 equals
    if line28 = $0 then line27
    else if line27 < line28 then line27 else line28

  definition net_ptc_credit equals line26
  definition excess_aptc_repayment equals line29
```
